def parse_user_from_xml(xml_string):
    data = xmltodict.parse(xml_string)
    user = data["user"]
    return {
        "name": user["name"],
        "email": user["email"],
        "role": user["@role"]
    }

instruction:
Write a function `order_to_xml(order_dict)` that uses `xmltodict.unparse()` to convert the given order dictionary into an XML string and **returns** it (with `pretty=True`).

Example input:
```python
order = {
    "order": {
        "@id": "1001",
        "customer": "Alice",
        "items": {
            "item": [
                {"@sku": "WM-001", "name": "Wireless Mouse", "qty": "1"},
                {"@sku": "KB-002", "name": "Keyboard", "qty": "2"}
            ]
        },
        "total": "109.97"
    }
}
```

